1. This project is for showcasing using machine learning (ML) in digital twin for injection molding process.
2. Injection molding needs the quick method to inspect injected parts quality so we can adjust processing conditions in real time.
3. We use ML to predict target, the part weight (PredictedPartWeight) from 4 parameter input-- InjectionPressure, MeltTemp, CoolingTime, PackingPressure.
4. We need these experimental data-- InjectionPressure, MeltTemp, CoolingTime, PackingPressure, and our target, ActualPartWeight so ML can learn fron them.
5. Files involved: gendata.py, injection_data_for_training.csv, injection_data_new.csv, injection_data_new4columns.csv, train_model.py, predict_manual.py, predict_batch.py

5.1 gendata.py 
Used: for generating 200 dataset for model training or for input data file. 
This file is made only just for testing. In real life, this file will not be used as we should get the dataset from the result of running injection experiment.
Command: python3 gendata.py
Output: injection_data_for_training.csv or injection_data_new.csv. 

5.2 injection_data_for_training.csv
Used: A text data file used for ML training. 
We should get this file from running injection experiment. There are 5 columns. The first line labels: InjectionPressure, MeltTemp, CoolingTime, PackingPressure, PartWeight. 
The 2nd line and so on are numeric data accordingly, separated by comma.

