5.3 injection_data_new.csv and injection_data_new4columns.csv
Used: for new input that users are expected to predict the target. 
This is own user data, being used as input for batch prediction in predict_batch.py. The injection_data_new.csv has 5 columns just like injection_data_for_training.csv. It could be exactly the same, if created with cp command or it can be generated from gendatafortraining.py.
The injection_data_new4columns.csv has only the first 4 columns refering 4 parameters. Use the first to compare with actual part weight while use the second when actual part weight is not available.

5.4 train_model.py
Used: for ML training and export 2 model files (injection_model.keras, scaler.pkl) 
These 2 model files will be used in the prediction step. Must have a file, injection_data_for_training.csv in the same folder.
Command: python3 train_model.py
Input: injection_data_for_training.csv
Output: injection_model.keras and scaler.pkl

5.5 predict_manual.py
Used: to predict part weight by entering InjectionPressure MeltTemp CoolingTime PackingPressure, separated by a space. Stop when entering "x". 
If part weight is over 50, suggest new injection pressure and packing pressure while keeping the same melt temp and cooling time.
Input: trained model files -- injection_model.keras, scaler.pkl
Output: predicted part weight, also new suggested parameters to make part weight lower than 50, in case the predicted part weight showed over 50.

